================================================================================
WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS, AND WHAT IT CANNOT
================================================================================

It covers the tools, the build system, the documentation and the C++ sources
written in this repository.

IT DOES NOT COVER, AND CANNOT GRANT ANY RIGHT TO:

  * SpongeBob's Truth or Square, its code, its data or its assets. That game
    is copyright its rightsholders. No part of it is distributed here: the
    retail image, the ripped disc and the Xbox 360 XDK are all gitignored and
    absent, and the build refuses to run without them. You must supply your
    own legally obtained copy.

  * The middleware the title links against -- Havok, FMOD, Ogg Vorbis and
    Bink -- each of which carries its own license from its own vendor.

  * `thirdparty/disasm/`, a copy of the GNU binutils PowerPC disassembler,
    which is GPL-licensed and carries its own terms. It is vendored for
    disassembly only and is not part of the MIT-licensed work above.

  * `thirdparty/ogg_vorbis/`, unmodified upstream libogg 1.1.3 and libvorbis
    1.2.0 from the Xiph.Org Foundation, which are BSD 3-clause licensed and
    carry their own terms in `ogg/COPYING` and `vorbis/COPYING`. They are
    vendored because the title's audio middleware links them and the matches
    that reproduce those bytes have to be rebuildable from a clone. They are
    not part of the MIT-licensed work above, and no claim is made over them.

Disassembly listings appear in comments throughout `src/` because a matching
decompilation is unreadable without them. They are excerpts of the original
program, quoted to document what each function must reproduce, and they are
not licensed by the notice above.
